## Additional Research Attribution

This project builds upon foundational works in quantum cryptography and machine learning:

1. Gisin, N., Ribordy, G., Tittel, W., & Zbinden, H. (2002). Quantum cryptography. 
   Reviews of modern physics, 74(1), 145-195.

2. Dunjko, V., & Briegel, H. J. (2018). Machine learning & artificial intelligence 
   in the quantum domain: a review of recent progress. Reports on Progress in Physics, 
   81(7), 074001.

3. Modern advances in quantum key distribution protocol design and optimization methods,
   as surveyed in contemporary quantum information literature.

## Research Use

This software is specifically designed for academic research and educational purposes
in the intersection of artificial intelligence and quantum cryptography. 

Commercial use is permitted under the MIT license terms, but we encourage users to:
- Cite the original research if used in academic publications
- Acknowledge the open-source contributions if used in commercial products
- Share improvements back with the research community when possible

## Quantum Cryptography Disclaimer

This software is designed for research and educational purposes. While based on 
theoretically secure quantum cryptographic principles, any production deployment 
should undergo additional security review and validation appropriate for the 
specific use case and threat model.

The security analysis provided by this software should be validated by qualified
cryptographic experts before use in security-critical applications.